                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Oh Apogee  <3  a name that contributed greatly to my childhood.\n\nMonster Bash is one of those classic Apogee platformer games that, while very difficult at times, you just can't help but love.\nThe art is still great, that charming cartoony style.\nThe music is catchy and fun.\nThe level design, while sometimes a little confusing, and more often than not, filled to the brim with awkward enemy placements that are specifically meant to cause you trouble, is great fun to explore and learn.\nSurprisingly decent length game too, for an old platformer. And, of course, tons of items scattered around for points, and secrets aplenty! Some nice extra challenge for completionists who like to 100% levels.\n\nSure the game frustrates me to no end sometimes, with its unexpected attacks out of nowhere, and damn near impossible to avoid tricks and traps, but I can't stay angry at it.\nIt's just so fun, and brings me back to those wonderful days!",
